# .gitleaks.toml IS committed, deliberately. It was ignored here back when it
# held the maintainer's address patterns; those now live in the PII_PATTERNS
# repository secret and the config carries no PII. Leaving it ignored meant CI
# ran gitleaks with default rules only while local runs used the project rules,
# so "gitleaks is clean" quietly meant two different things. Do not re-add it.

